One of my favorite monsters in the game is the nurse, because in a game
where good equipment can make you nigh invulnerable, the most dangerous
creature is the one who gets you to voluntarily remove all your nice
equipment.  A few of my most dangerous close-calls have been with
nurses... either letting a green slime sneak up on me or having a L pop
up and summon in a big crowd of nasties while I fumble with my dressing
maneuver.

So this is an idea to give the same kind of "you might get something
good, but there are many ways to screw it up and it might be really
bad" feel to another monster... the troublesome R class.

The idea is simple: if you engage a confused rust-monster in combat,
you have a chance of fixing rust.  If engage a confused disenchanter in
combat, you have a chance of having things enchanted or
rust/fireproofed.

To balance the obvious boon to characters, it makes R more dangerous
because characters are:
- less likely to genocide R
- less likely to attack R with ranged magic or throwaway weapons
- more likely to let R attack
- still in danger of armor/weapon vaporization by overenchantment.
- still in danger of confusion wearing off of monster in mid-fight.

To make it interesting and provide balance, there could be limited odds
to something good happening, and maybe even a possibility of a negative
effect even if the monster is confused.

Also of note, for good or bad: this would leave a possible avenue for
illiterate conducts to have enchanted armor/weapons.  (I don't think
there is currently, aside from lucky random pickups, is there?)



